package Patterns;

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Q10 {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner input = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Please enter n: ");
        int n = input.nextInt();

        for(int i = 1; i<=n; i++){
            for(int j = 1; j<=i; j++){
                System.out.print("* ");
            }
            System.out.println();
        }
        for (int i = 1; i <=n ; i++) {
            for (int j = 1; j <=n-i; j++) {
                System.out.print("* ");

            }
            System.out.println();
        }
    }
}

OUTPUT:
Please enter n: 5
* 
* * 
* * * 
* * * * 
* * * * * 
* * * * 
* * * 
* * 
* 


Approach
The pattern is printed in two parts:

1. Increasing Triangle
   - For each row i, print i stars.
   - Number of stars increases from 1 to n.

2. Decreasing Triangle
   - For each row i, print (n - i) stars.
   - Number of stars decreases from n - 1 to 0.

 Logic
- The first loop creates the upper half by increasing the star count row by row.
- The second loop creates the lower half by decreasing the star count row by row.
- Together, they form a symmetric star pattern.
 Time Complexity
- O(n²)

 Space Complexity
- O(1)
